melonDS 1.1 + GDB "monitor" commands for savestates and emulation speed (ARM9 stub).
Apply to tag 1.1 with `git apply`; build_melonds.sh (next to this file) clones, patches and builds it.

  monitor savestate <abs path>   -> OK | E.savestate failed
  monitor loadstate <abs path>   -> OK | E.state file not found | E.loadstate failed
  monitor fps <n>                -> OK | E01   (n > 0: limit to n frames/s, 0: unlimited)
  monitor reset                  -> OK         (stock)
  anything else                  -> E01

savestate/loadstate run on the emulator thread at the end of the current frame (like the
menu items), and the reply is only sent once the state is written/loaded. If the target
was halted when the command arrived, it runs to the end of that frame, does the operation
and halts again without sending a stop reply: the client keeps reading/writing memory and
resumes with `c` as usual. fps applies immediately (it does not persist to the config and
needs AudioSync off, the default).

The GDB stub also works with the JIT enabled now, minus breakpoints/watchpoints/stepping:
requests are served and halts happen at the start of each frame.

